# 1. Purpose and Scope

This document specifies the functional requirements for the Budget Planning module of the OPEX Budgeting System (OBS). It defines what the system must do — the business rules, data rules, access control behaviours, and acceptance criteria that govern budget line entry, budget version management, vendor attribution, overhead allocation, calculation rules, budget entry locking, and budget submission.

This specification resolves the following open items from predecessor documents:

- **Security and Access Control Specification v1.1 — Section 10 placeholder:** budget entry locking mechanics.

- **Data Integration Specification v1.2 — OI-DI-06:** cost center hierarchy maintenance boundary.

- **Project Context Handoff v1.4 — open item:** complex business rules (compensation burden rates, overhead allocation formulas, fiscal calendar logic).

All architectural decisions recorded in the Application Architecture Specification v3.6, Security and Access Control Specification v1.4, UX and UI Specification v1.5, and Data Integration Specification v1.6 are final and are not re-litigated here. This document adds functional detail on top of those decisions without contradicting them.

## 1.1 In Scope

- Budget line entry and editing — non-personnel expense accounts.

- Budget line derivation — personnel expense accounts (read-only, sourced from Workforce Planning).

- Overhead allocation — calculated read-only budget lines derived from headcount and geography-based rates.

- Vendor attribution — per-period vendor line items on designated expense accounts.

- Budget version management — creation (via clone), naming, activation, archiving, and deletion.

- Budget target management — per cost center / expense account / planning period / budget version.

- Calculation service rules — compensation burden rates and overhead allocation rates.

- Budget entry locking — granularity, authority, locked-state permissions, and audit events.

- Budget entry workflow — guided three-step entry process (personnel → non-personnel → review and submit).

- Budget submission — status transitions, mandatory commentary, Finance routing.

- Cost center hierarchy maintenance boundary — OBS-managed changes post initial import, including bulk cost center upload.

- PostgreSQL schema additions and API endpoint requirements for all of the above.

## 1.2 Out of Scope

- Finance-side approval workflow — fully specified in Functional Requirements: Finance Approval Workflow v1.2.

- Workforce planning functional requirements — covered in Functional Requirements: Workforce Planning v1.1.

- Reporting functional requirements — covered in Functional Requirements: Reporting v1.1.

- Account hierarchy maintenance — the account hierarchy is read-only in OBS; the ingestion pipeline is the only write path (Data Integration Specification v1.6).

